1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:08,341
In September twenty twenty-three, inside Mexico's Congress, two small boxes were opened in front of the cameras.

2
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:13,633
Inside lay two tiny bodies with long heads and three fingers on each hand.

3
00:00:14,099 --> 00:00:18,911
The man presenting them said, under oath, that they were not human.

4
00:00:18,911 --> 00:00:20,563
Not from our evolution.

5
00:00:20,563 --> 00:00:22,071
A thousand years old.

6
00:00:22,071 --> 00:00:24,800
Found in the desert of Nazca, in Peru.

7
00:00:25,266 --> 00:00:27,944
The clip went around the world in hours.

8
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:29,952
Aliens, shown to a parliament.

9
00:00:29,952 --> 00:00:33,500
For millions of people, that sounded like disclosure.

10
00:00:33,966 --> 00:00:36,615
But a parliament is not a laboratory.

11
00:00:36,615 --> 00:00:40,337
Science has its own test for an extraordinary claim.

12
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:45,133
You submit it, and experts tear it apart before anyone believes it.

13
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,831
So tonight we do exactly that.

14
00:00:51,831 --> 00:00:55,253
We send the Nazca mummies out for peer review.

15
00:00:55,253 --> 00:00:56,295
Five referees.

16
00:00:56,295 --> 00:00:58,527
One rebuttal from the authors.

17
00:00:58,527 --> 00:01:00,833
And then the editor's decision.

18
00:01:01,299 --> 00:01:02,852
First, the submission.

19
00:01:02,852 --> 00:01:06,028
The claim, as its authors make it, is simple.

20
00:01:06,028 --> 00:01:14,425
In the deserts around Nazca and Palpa, a group of three-fingered beings was found, preserved for over a thousand years.

21
00:01:14,425 --> 00:01:15,766
They are not human.

22
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:18,855
Every paper needs a methods section.

23
00:01:18,855 --> 00:01:22,423
Where were the specimens found, by whom, and how?

24
00:01:22,423 --> 00:01:24,171
Here the trouble starts.

25
00:01:24,171 --> 00:01:26,502
No archaeologist excavated them.

26
00:01:26,502 --> 00:01:26,866
Ever.

27
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:34,150
According to the people who promoted them, the bodies came from huaqueros, tomb looters from Palpa.

28
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:36,697
Their leader was known only as Mario.

29
00:01:36,697 --> 00:01:42,000
One of the promoters called him a delinquent, well known to the local police.

30
00:01:42,466 --> 00:01:49,447
In January twenty seventeen, the French explorer Thierry Jamin wrote to Peru's Ministry of Culture.

31
00:01:49,447 --> 00:01:55,723
He described about twenty humanoid bodies in stone sarcophagi, with three-fingered hands.

32
00:01:55,723 --> 00:02:00,800
Then he raised money online, almost forty thousand euros, to study them.

33
00:02:01,266 --> 00:02:10,843
In June twenty seventeen, a streaming site released a series about the largest body, a pale, white-powdered figure the team called Maria.

34
00:02:10,843 --> 00:02:15,666
Gaia, the site, said she might be around seventeen hundred years old.

35
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:27,245
Six years later, smaller bodies, about sixty centimetres tall, reached Mexico's Congress, presented by the journalist and UFO researcher Jaime Maussan.

36
00:02:27,245 --> 00:02:28,717
The claim had grown.

37
00:02:28,717 --> 00:02:31,366
Non-human, and possibly intelligent.

38
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:34,185
Editor's note on the submission.

39
00:02:34,185 --> 00:02:39,917
A specimen bought from looters has no context: no grave, no layers, no record.

40
00:02:39,917 --> 00:02:41,828
Science can still test it.

41
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:45,135
But every test now has to work twice as hard.

42
00:02:45,135 --> 00:02:47,266
Send it to the first referee.

43
00:02:47,733 --> 00:02:50,067
Referee one is a radiologist.

44
00:02:50,067 --> 00:02:54,655
Because the strongest card the authors hold is the scans.

45
00:02:54,655 --> 00:03:00,933
X-rays and CT scans, published for years, showing skeletons inside the bodies.

46
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,408
And it's true.

47
00:03:02,408 --> 00:03:04,424
There are real bones inside.

48
00:03:04,424 --> 00:03:10,544
Promoters point to skeletons with no obvious seams, organs, even what they call eggs.

49
00:03:10,544 --> 00:03:13,497
To them, that is the end of the argument.

50
00:03:13,497 --> 00:03:16,233
To a radiologist, it is the beginning.

51
00:03:16,699 --> 00:03:18,177
Look at Maria first.

52
00:03:18,177 --> 00:03:28,226
Anthropologist Andrew Nelson said she looks like a typical Nazca mummy, sitting in the flexed position Nazca people used for their dead.

53
00:03:28,226 --> 00:03:29,260
A human being.

54
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:32,733
Wrapped and buried by her family centuries ago.

55
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:37,112
The hands and feet are where the scans get interesting.

56
00:03:37,112 --> 00:03:47,500
Experts reading the images say they show signs of manipulation: digits removed, bones rearranged, and a white powder coating that hides the joins.

57
00:03:47,966 --> 00:03:53,966
Then a three-fingered hand came into the hands of Peru's own forensic institute.

58
00:03:53,966 --> 00:03:58,166
The X-rays showed human bones from adults and juveniles.

59
00:03:58,166 --> 00:04:01,466
One finger bone had been glued in backwards.

60
00:04:01,933 --> 00:04:02,857
And the eggs?

61
00:04:02,857 --> 00:04:10,533
In one sixty centimetre figure seized by Peruvian authorities, the eggs on the scan turned out to be stones.

62
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:11,995
Reviewer note.

63
00:04:11,995 --> 00:04:13,987
A scan shows what is inside.

64
00:04:13,987 --> 00:04:16,904
It cannot tell you whether it grew there.

65
00:04:16,904 --> 00:04:23,733
Real bones are what you would expect, whether the body is alien, or assembled from real remains.

66
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:26,279
Referee two is an anatomist.

67
00:04:26,279 --> 00:04:30,288
The job: does this body make sense as a living animal?

68
00:04:30,288 --> 00:04:33,332
Every vertebrate on Earth follows a plan.

69
00:04:33,332 --> 00:04:38,233
Bones meet in predictable ways, because they have to carry weight.

70
00:04:38,699 --> 00:04:51,402
In January twenty twenty-four, forensic archaeologist Flavio Estrada showed what was inside two small figures seized at a Lima courier office, on their way to Mexico.

71
00:04:51,402 --> 00:04:54,693
The head of one was the skull of a camelid.

72
00:04:54,693 --> 00:04:56,300
A llama or an alpaca.

73
00:04:56,766 --> 00:04:58,000
The arms and legs?

74
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,753
Bird bones.

75
00:04:58,753 --> 00:05:05,262
The snout of the skull had been cut away, and a face was modelled on the back of the braincase.

76
00:05:05,262 --> 00:05:10,333
Metal plates had been placed on the chest, to look mysterious on an X-ray.

77
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,878
Estrada's verdict was blunt.

78
00:05:12,878 --> 00:05:15,253
These are not extraterrestrials.

79
00:05:15,253 --> 00:05:16,886
Not intraterrestrials.

80
00:05:16,886 --> 00:05:18,222
Not a new species.

81
00:05:18,222 --> 00:05:19,113
Not hybrids.

82
00:05:19,113 --> 00:05:25,199
In his words, they are dolls assembled from the bones of animals from this planet.

83
00:05:25,666 --> 00:05:30,962
He also noted something any anatomist would: there is no evolutionary logic.

84
00:05:30,962 --> 00:05:37,233
With those flat feet and those joints, the figures could never have walked, or even stood.

85
00:05:37,699 --> 00:05:39,283
The authors push back.

86
00:05:39,283 --> 00:05:45,327
A report by Cliff Miles proposes the small bodies are a brand-new genus and species.

87
00:05:45,327 --> 00:05:51,300
And promoters insist the seized figures were cheap folk dolls, not their specimens.

88
00:05:51,766 --> 00:05:52,772
Reviewer note.

89
00:05:52,772 --> 00:05:54,929
That objection cuts both ways.

90
00:05:54,929 --> 00:06:01,182
If the authors' bodies are different, they must be opened to the same independent test.

91
00:06:01,182 --> 00:06:06,933
Until then, the only small figures examined by a state lab were built, not born.

92
00:06:07,399 --> 00:06:09,358
Referee three is a chemist.

93
00:06:09,358 --> 00:06:10,590
Forget the bones.

94
00:06:10,590 --> 00:06:12,404
What is the skin made of?

95
00:06:12,404 --> 00:06:18,133
A body that is a thousand years old should be made of a thousand-year-old body.

96
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:25,879
Peru's forensic team used infrared spectroscopy, which reads the chemical fingerprint of a material.

97
00:06:25,879 --> 00:06:34,833
On the three-fingered hand, they found wool, polypropylene plastic, and a glue so specific they matched it to a brand: UHU.

98
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:42,461
The so-called skin of the small figures was a paste of glues, plant fibre and ground paper.

99
00:06:42,461 --> 00:06:46,160
Estrada's team looked for cells and found none.

100
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:48,600
Just fibre, gum, glue and oils.

101
00:06:49,066 --> 00:06:50,622
Then the white powder.

102
00:06:50,622 --> 00:06:58,964
The authors told Congress the beings were buried in diatomaceous earth, fossil algae, and that is what preserved them.

103
00:06:58,964 --> 00:06:59,388
Maybe.

104
00:06:59,388 --> 00:07:04,266
But a white coat over everything is also exactly how you hide a join.

105
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:05,728
Reviewer note.

106
00:07:05,728 --> 00:07:09,496
Modern synthetic glue cannot be a thousand years old.

107
00:07:09,496 --> 00:07:13,833
Whatever is ancient in these objects, the assembly is recent.

108
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:17,077
Referee four runs a radiocarbon lab.

109
00:07:17,077 --> 00:07:27,800
And this is the evidence Congress heard most about: a carbon-fourteen date from Mexico's national university, UNAM, about a thousand years.

110
00:07:28,266 --> 00:07:30,695
Here is what the lab actually did.

111
00:07:30,695 --> 00:07:37,695
In May twenty seventeen, a client sent samples which, the client said, were skin and brain tissue.

112
00:07:37,695 --> 00:07:38,980
About half a gram.

113
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,338
The lab dated them.

114
00:07:40,338 --> 00:07:41,266
That was all.

115
00:07:41,733 --> 00:07:46,702
When the date was used in Congress, the university reissued its statement.

116
00:07:46,702 --> 00:07:50,597
Its staff never took the samples and never saw the source.

117
00:07:50,597 --> 00:07:55,633
It rejects any use or interpretation of its results beyond the date itself.

118
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:58,830
And think about what an old date means.

119
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:03,662
Peru's desert is full of real burials more than a thousand years old.

120
00:08:03,662 --> 00:08:07,933
Old tissue is exactly what you would get from a looted grave.

121
00:08:08,399 --> 00:08:09,389
Reviewer note.

122
00:08:09,389 --> 00:08:14,480
Radiocarbon dates the material in the tube, not the object on the table.

123
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:20,066
An ancient date is fully consistent with ancient human remains, reworked today.

124
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:22,627
Referee five is a geneticist.

125
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:25,444
This is the test that should settle it.

126
00:08:25,444 --> 00:08:28,622
Alien life would not share our genetic code.

127
00:08:28,622 --> 00:08:30,066
Human remains would.

128
00:08:30,533 --> 00:08:37,669
The promoters' own sequencing has circulated since twenty eighteen, with headlines about unknown DNA.

129
00:08:37,669 --> 00:08:41,838
Large shares of the reads could not be matched to anything.

130
00:08:41,838 --> 00:08:44,100
That sounded like a smoking gun.

131
00:08:44,566 --> 00:08:46,479
But unknown is not alien.

132
00:08:46,479 --> 00:08:53,825
Old, dirty, handled tissue is full of bacteria and broken fragments that databases cannot place.

133
00:08:53,825 --> 00:09:00,100
Even the promoters' reports said most identifiable reads were human contamination.

134
00:09:00,566 --> 00:09:04,439
The raw data was public, so anyone could check it.

135
00:09:04,439 --> 00:09:13,966
In December twenty twenty-five, bioinformatician Alaina Hardie and Alan Izarraras-Gomez of UNAM published their reanalysis.

136
00:09:14,433 --> 00:09:18,930
Their conclusion: the DNA is unambiguously modern human.

137
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:24,070
It lacks the damage patterns that real ancient DNA always shows.

138
00:09:24,070 --> 00:09:28,166
The most likely source is contamination in the lab.

139
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:29,632
Reviewer note.

140
00:09:29,632 --> 00:09:32,486
The genetic signal is human, and modern.

141
00:09:32,486 --> 00:09:37,266
Nothing in the published sequence data requires a non-human source.

142
00:09:37,733 --> 00:09:40,643
Now the authors get their right of reply.

143
00:09:40,643 --> 00:09:51,433
In November twenty twenty-three, at a second session in Mexico's Congress, a line of doctors testified that the bodies were real, once-living organisms.

144
00:09:51,899 --> 00:09:59,735
In twenty twenty-four, an American lawyer and his team said Maria's fingerprints did not look like human prints.

145
00:09:59,735 --> 00:10:01,484
Preliminary, he stressed.

146
00:10:01,484 --> 00:10:09,599
In twenty twenty-five, a Russian doctor self-published a CT study arguing the bodies looked biologically consistent.

147
00:10:10,066 --> 00:10:21,321
In January twenty twenty-six, the promoters said six bodies were handed to a university in Ica, which asked for them to be registered as cultural heritage.

148
00:10:21,321 --> 00:10:23,500
Research, they say, continues.

149
00:10:23,966 --> 00:10:25,619
And there was a lawsuit.

150
00:10:25,619 --> 00:10:30,303
Maussan announced a three hundred million dollar claim against Peru.

151
00:10:30,303 --> 00:10:40,015
The court record tells a quieter story: declared inadmissible in twenty twenty-five, rejected on appeal, archived in April twenty twenty-six.

152
00:10:40,015 --> 00:10:41,600
It never reached trial.

153
00:10:42,066 --> 00:10:44,041
And the theory keeps moving.

154
00:10:44,041 --> 00:10:51,233
In October twenty twenty-six, Maussan floated a new idea: maybe the bodies are humans from the future.

155
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,923
Editor's reading of the rebuttal.

156
00:10:53,923 --> 00:11:04,500
It offers many voices, but no one has handed a specimen, with a documented chain of custody, to an independent lab that publishes in a peer-reviewed journal.

157
00:11:04,966 --> 00:11:08,566
There is one more referee the authors never asked for.

158
00:11:08,566 --> 00:11:09,100
History.

159
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:16,566
In the nineteenth century, scientists measured Andean skulls to argue that ancient Peruvians were somehow other.

160
00:11:16,566 --> 00:11:20,566
The historian Christopher Heaney sees the same pattern here.

161
00:11:21,033 --> 00:11:26,463
Ancient Peruvians built cities, irrigation, and the giant lines in the desert.

162
00:11:26,463 --> 00:11:34,399
Every alien story about Nazca quietly takes that achievement away from them, and gives it to someone from the sky.

163
00:11:34,866 --> 00:11:39,042
Peru's mummy experts said it most clearly in twenty seventeen.

164
00:11:39,042 --> 00:11:45,643
These finds, they wrote, are without any doubt human remains, the cultural heritage of the nation.

165
00:11:45,643 --> 00:11:51,166
One of them added: you cannot take away the condition of human from a human being.

166
00:11:51,633 --> 00:11:54,989
Because that is the part the clip never showed.

167
00:11:54,989 --> 00:11:59,702
If the large bodies are real Nazca mummies, they were real people.

168
00:11:59,702 --> 00:12:01,273
Someone's grandmother.

169
00:12:01,273 --> 00:12:02,415
Someone's child.

170
00:12:02,415 --> 00:12:06,200
Taken from their graves and reshaped to sell a story.

171
00:12:06,666 --> 00:12:09,943
Peru has treated it as a crime from the start.

172
00:12:09,943 --> 00:12:15,641
Prosecutors opened a case on looted archaeological material in twenty seventeen.

173
00:12:15,641 --> 00:12:21,766
One man linked to the first finds was given a suspended sentence in twenty twenty-two.

174
00:12:22,233 --> 00:12:24,299
Five referee reports are in.

175
00:12:24,299 --> 00:12:26,145
The authors have replied.

176
00:12:26,145 --> 00:12:28,433
Time for the editor's decision.

177
00:12:28,899 --> 00:12:30,633
Here is how the claim scored.

178
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:36,486
The large bodies are best explained as real ancient human mummies: evidence.

179
00:12:36,486 --> 00:12:42,582
The small figures examined by Peru's state lab were built from animal bones: evidence.

180
00:12:42,582 --> 00:12:46,764
The three-fingered hand was human bones and glue: evidence.

181
00:12:46,764 --> 00:12:50,733
And an old carbon date proves an alien origin: debunked.

182
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:57,698
Unknown DNA proves a non-human being: debunked, it is modern human contamination.

183
00:12:57,698 --> 00:13:02,272
Every specimen independently tested: not yet, still open.

184
00:13:02,272 --> 00:13:07,166
And the core claim, non-human beings from Nazca: no evidence.

185
00:13:07,633 --> 00:13:08,996
Decision: rejected.

186
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:12,154
Not because the idea of alien life is silly.

187
00:13:12,154 --> 00:13:12,800
It isn't.

188
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:20,766
But because every test this claim could be put through, it failed, and every time it failed, the story changed.

189
00:13:21,233 --> 00:13:23,586
So what do the scans really show?

190
00:13:23,586 --> 00:13:24,371
Real bones.

191
00:13:24,371 --> 00:13:27,580
Some from humans, some from llamas and birds.

192
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:33,000
Joined with modern glue, wrapped in paper paste, and coated in white powder.

193
00:13:33,466 --> 00:13:37,386
What they don't show is anything that never lived on Earth.

194
00:13:37,386 --> 00:13:39,779
The mystery was never in the bodies.

195
00:13:39,779 --> 00:13:43,500
It was in how a looted grave can end up in a parliament.

196
00:13:43,966 --> 00:13:50,143
If we ever do find life beyond Earth, it will not arrive in a box from a tomb raider.

197
00:13:50,143 --> 00:13:55,520
It will come through the slow, boring, beautiful process you just watched.

198
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:56,319
Submission.

199
00:13:56,319 --> 00:13:56,828
Review.

200
00:13:56,828 --> 00:13:57,700
Replication.

201
00:13:58,166 --> 00:14:03,427
And the people inside these bodies deserve what every one of us would want.

202
00:14:03,427 --> 00:14:05,321
A name, if it can be found.

203
00:14:05,321 --> 00:14:05,883
A grave.

204
00:14:05,883 --> 00:14:07,566
And to be left in peace.

205
00:14:08,033 --> 00:14:11,115
This has been a case file from Ancient Machines.

206
00:14:11,115 --> 00:14:16,379
If you want the next claim sent out for review, tell me in the comments which one.

207
00:14:16,379 --> 00:14:19,333
And subscribe, so you don't miss the decision.
